hello my name is matthias from datatab  and in this video i'd like to show you  how you can easily  create a frequency table online with  datatab  but first of all what is a frequency  table a frequency table  are created in statistics if you want to  display  the absolute and the relative  frequencies  of the characteristics of your variables  a frequency table  thus provides you with a table that  shows you how  often each value occurred in your data  a frequency table for the variable  gender for example  shows you how often the male and female  values  occur in your sample so let's have a  look at this  simple example you ask nine people what  their favorite  candy is two of them answer cake  four of them answer ice and three of  them  answer donut so then this will be your  frequency table  cake you have the frequency 2 eyes say  frequency 4  and donut the frequency 3 and  in total you have 9 people ask  so and here at the right side you can  see the  percentage so cake has 22 percent  ice 44 percent and doughnut  33 so now let's create  a frequency table by our own with data  tab first of all  if you want to use your own data you  must click on clear  table afterwards you can copy your own  data  into this table so i select this data  and copy them into the table so  in this example you simply ask 12  students  what is their favorite car print in  order to create a frequency table  you need to click on the tab descriptive  and now  you want to create a frequency table for  the variable  car brand so you simply click on the  variable  car brand further you want to calculate  the frequencies  and you can simply click on frequencies  now you will see here it's left  the frequency table for the car brand  further you can click on  percent and valid percent now you can  see here  the frequencies of the car brands  there's one  invalid value here we don't have any  value  so we have one invalid value and  here you can see the percentage of the  carbons  and the valid percentage of the carb  brands  if you liked this video please subscribe  to our youtube channel  if you have questions or feedback just  leave us a comment  thanks and bye matthias
 

